data stick_capacity_bytes: std.measure.ByteSize = byte_size(34359738368)

// PROVENANCE, SPLIT BY WHAT ACTUALLY SUPPORTS EACH FACT, because the module scope binds its
// citation to this exact declaration and a generic DDR4 reference cannot carry a vendor SKU.
// No first-party Samsung document for this part was reachable: it is an EOL SKU, and the
// per-part paths under semiconductor.samsung.com now serve a generic DDR overview rather than
// a datasheet (checked 2026-08-12). So the exact figures below are LABEL facts supplied with
// the operator's procurement brief — 32GB, DDR4-2133, LRDIMM, 4Rx4 — and not a reading of a
// vendor datasheet. The module anchor cites DDR4 only. Load reduction is NOT cited here: it is
// grounded where DimmBuffering is declared, in extdeps.memory.types, which is the single place
// the Registered-memory citation belongs and the reason the duplicate anchor once carried in
// this module was deleted. A generic source can honestly support what DDR4 and load reduction
// MEAN; neither source says anything about this part.
// Dissolve-on: a Samsung product-selection guide or module datasheet carrying this part row,
// at which point these become cited facts and the label stops being the authority.
//
// WHAT THE MODEL ADDS IS A CHECK, NOT A RESTATEMENT. capacity, chip_width and rank_count are
// independent label facts, and dram_module_required_die_density divides them back out to a
// 4 Gbit die — which is the density the module is independently described as carrying. Three
// label numbers that could each have been mistyped agree on a fourth that was not authored
// here, so the row is corroborated rather than merely transcribed.
//
// ONE PRECISION, since the derived count reads as a package count and is not one: at x4 with
// ECC the module carries 18 dies per rank and 72 across four ranks, which this part reaches
// as 36 dual-die packages. dram_chips_per_rank counts DIES, the unit that determines density.
data m386a4g40dm0_cpb_catalog: extdeps.memory.types.DramModuleCatalogRow = extdeps.memory.types.DramModuleCatalogRow {
  part_number: "M386A4G40DM0-CPB",
  manufacturer: samsung,
  generation: dram_generation_ddr4,
  capacity_bytes: stick_capacity_bytes,
  data_rate_mts: 2133,
  ecc: true,
  buffering: LoadReduced,
  chip_width: bit_width(4),

  rank_count: 4,
}
